                                <p>The manuscript is in three hands. First (main) hand copied fols. 1-2, 6–28. Second hand: fol. 5 (according to Sfardata). Third hand: fols. 3-4. According to Sfardata, hand 2 also copies a number of folios in Yevr.-Arab I 0832. None of the folios written by hand 2 in Yevr.-Arab I 0756 and Yevr.-Arab I 0832 appears (in the images) to be physically connected with the folios in hand 1 and hand 3.<lb/>Folio 3 in hand 3 appears to be physically connected with folio 2 in hand 1.</p>
